eer AI doesn't undermine the claim that AI is a net positive — it just means the net positive isn't automatic. But very few good things in history have been automatic. Democracy isn't automatic; it requires participation, laws, and vigilance. Public health isn't automatic; it requires sanitation systems, vaccines, and regulation. The same is true for AI. The technology opens a door, but we have to walk through it together. So my stance is not that AI will magically make everything better. It's that AI gives us more tools, more leverage, and more potential to create a better world — including more and better employment opportunities — than we would have without it. And that potential, combined with human effort, is what makes it a net positive in the long term. I don't think that's undermined by acknowledging the need for policy. If anything, it's strengthened by it — because it means we have agency, not just inevitability.
